{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqijq7y4kc9","workspace":"D:/zonoid","title":"background subagent that polls a long job burns its turn budget and dies without reporting","summary":"ROOT CAUSE of the recurring \"subagent never reported / hung\" pattern, confirmed on the #31 pilot. The pilot RUN completed cleanly — pilot.log ends \"PILOT COMPLETE in 22.8 min\" with all results written to disk — but the dispatching Agent was instructed to launch the run via Bash run_in_background and POLL until done. Each poll is one Agent turn; a ~23-min run is dozens of poll-turns, which exhausts the subagent's turn/token budget, so it is terminated around when the run finishes — BEFORE reaching read-results/complete_task/report. The work succeeds; the messenger dies mid-poll, leaving the task in_progress with no completion notification. (Process census confirmed: no old claude-code process survived; results were recovered by reading the files directly.) FIX: never have a subagent babysit a long background job by polling. For runs >10 min the MAIN loop launches the background Bash itself (the harness re-invokes the main loop on completion — no turn-burning poll) and reads results; or the run writes a DONE sentinel and results are read off disk regardless of the worker. Short (<10 min) work stays inline in a single foreground Bash.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-17T20:51:18.076Z","vec":[0.005824348423629999,0.0016557624330744147,-0.058564938604831696,0.022109663113951683,0.06203721836209297,-0.031445205211639404,-0.030434198677539825,0.00857273768633604,0.02612150087952614,0.07440435886383057,-0.03995586559176445,0.02617928571999073,-0.06391410529613495,-0.014209894463419914,-0.008925740607082844,-0.002232092432677746,0.042702436447143555,-0.08901571482419968,-0.04887915030121803,-0.04283512756228447,-0.004267268348485231,0.04065357893705368,0.0847381204366684,0.0317988321185112,-0.03691458702087402,-0.015830889344215393,-0.05406465753912926,-0.07924557477235794,0.0210922